From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 21:48:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: dw-hdmi: Respect the HDMI 1.4 TMDS limit for deep
 color

Deep color output was only checked against the maximum TMDS clock of
the HDMI Forum data block when the sink has one. A 2560x1440 mode at
241.5 MHz then went out as 10-bit RGB at 301.875 MHz to a sink which
declares 300 MHz in its HDMI vendor specific data block, which left the
screen black.

Also check unscrambled rates against the HDMI 1.4 limit.

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
index c23c30974a08..840abeb16e57 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
@@ -2738,6 +2738,15 @@ static bool dw_hdmi_deep_color_fits(struct dw_hdmi *hdmi,
 	else
 		max = min(max, 165000U);
 
+	/*
+	 * The HDMI Forum data block only covers rates above 340 MHz, where
+	 * scrambling is used. Below that, the limit of the HDMI vendor
+	 * specific data block still applies, which some sinks set lower.
+	 */
+	if (tmds <= 340000 && info->hdmi.max_tmds_clock_14 &&
+	    tmds > info->hdmi.max_tmds_clock_14)
+		return false;
+
 	return tmds <= max;
 }
 
